    "result_text": "The full test suite is green \u2014 all 23 tests pass, including the new `Cp14Tests`.\n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented the `membershipNumber` field formatted as `<customerCode>-M<YY>`, where `YY` is the last two digits of the `registrationDate` year (e.g. `SMI-0007-M26`).\n\nSince `membershipNumber` is derived purely from the owner's own fields (the Cp14 spec explicitly calls it \"seed-independent\"), I followed the existing pattern for the other computed read-only fields (`displayName`, `initials`) rather than adding a persisted column:\n\n1. **`src/main/resources/openapi.yml`** \u2014 Added `membershipNumber` as a `readOnly` string property on the `Owner` schema, so the OpenAPI generator produces the field on `OwnerDto` at build time.\n\n2. **`src/main/java/.../mapper/OwnerMapper.java`** \u2014 Added a `@Mapping` that populates `membershipNumber` from a new `membershipNumber(Owner)` helper: `String.format(\"%s-M%02d\", customerCode, registrationDate.getYear() % 100)`. It returns `null` when either source field is absent, so the 10 seeded owners (which have no `customer_code`/`registration_date`) still serialize cleanly on any GET.\n\nNo entity or database schema changes were needed. The `%02d` formatting correctly matches the test's `registrationDate.substring(2,4)` extraction, including years like 2005 \u2192 `05`.",
